WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.776
Forty-seven gigabytes

00:00:01.624 --> 00:00:02.885
of mystery System

00:00:02.697 --> 00:00:03.298
Data

00:00:03.822 --> 00:00:05.154
One developer's Mac

00:00:04.966 --> 00:00:06.227
reported forty-seven

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.265
gigabytes of System

00:00:07.077 --> 00:00:07.642
Data

00:00:07.737 --> 00:00:08.397
and none of

00:00:08.209 --> 00:00:09.234
it was photos

00:00:09.046 --> 00:00:10.036
or downloads

00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:11.560
It was developer

00:00:11.372 --> 00:00:12.208
leftovers

00:00:12.421 --> 00:00:13.659
Xcode build data

00:00:13.754 --> 00:00:14.862
Docker images

00:00:15.004 --> 00:00:16.289
old node modules

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.480
and package caches

00:00:17.645 --> 00:00:18.352
most of it

00:00:18.164 --> 00:00:19.473
rebuildable again with

00:00:19.284 --> 00:00:20.581
a single command

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.018
The piece maps

00:00:21.829 --> 00:00:22.937
the folders behind

00:00:22.749 --> 00:00:23.610
the bloat and

00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:24.329
the commands to

00:00:24.141 --> 00:00:25.390
clear them safely

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:26.829
starting with measuring

00:00:26.641 --> 00:00:27.525
first what is

00:00:27.336 --> 00:00:28.291
actually there

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.844
Full story on

00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:30.551
the dashboard
